r=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;out=r/'results';a=json.loads((out/'comparison.json').read_text());old=json.loads((r.parent/'analysis/comparison.json').read_text());commit=a['commit'];url='https://github.com/Faheemibrahim/unitree_go2_ros2/blob/'+commit+'/';raw=a['raw_vendor'];cor=a['default_corrected_vendor'];hy=a['optional_lio_hybrid'];native=a['unfiltered_optional_lio'];guard=a['guard'];adapter=json.loads((out/'input_adapter_audit.json').read_text());lines=['# real-go2 branch: odometry comparison on the lab recording','',f"Pinned branch: `real-go2`, commit `{commit}`. Source: `/home/jain/go2_bags/go2_20261018_173219`, 217.353 s; approximate physical return to original position and heading.",'','| Odometry path | Estimated horizontal return offset | Estimated heading change |','|---|---:|---:|',f"| Original vendor `/utlidar/robot_odom` | {raw['horizontal_return_offset_m']:.3f} m | {raw['heading_return_change_deg']:.2f} degrees |",f"| Repository default: vendor plus yaw correction | **{cor['horizontal_return_offset_m']:.3f} m** | {cor['heading_return_change_deg']:.2f} degrees |",f"| Repository optional LIO with guarded vendor bridge | {hy['horizontal_return_offset_m']:.3f} m | {hy['heading_return_change_deg']:.2f} degrees |",f"| Repository optional LIO before its guard, anchored at first output | {native['horizontal_return_offset_imu_m']:.3f} m | {native['heading_return_change_deg']:.2f} degrees |",f"| Previous standalone raw-cloud/body-IMU Point-LIO test | {old['return_checks']['point_lio']['horizontal_return_offset_m']:.3f} m | {old['return_checks']['point_lio']['heading_return_change_deg']:.2f} degrees |",'', 'Approximate endpoint placement is not surveyed ground truth: these are estimated return offsets, not pure drift measurements. All comparison poses refer to the same developer-URDF IMU lever arm.','', '![Paths and returns](results/comparison.png)','','## What the branch actually runs','', f"[real_mapping.launch.py]({url}unitree_go2_real/launch/real_mapping.launch.py) defaults to `lio:=false`. Its [real_bridge.yaml]({url}unitree_go2_real/config/real_bridge.yaml) sets `yaw_scale: 0.9814`. [real_tf_bridge.py]({url}unitree_go2_real/scripts/real_tf_bridge.py) converts each vendor position increment into the body frame, scales its yaw increment, and integrates the step at the corrected heading. It is not a new scan-matching odometry estimator in this default mode. The parameter is used as published, without fitting to this bag.",'',f"With `lio:=true`, the branch uses [lio_input.py]({url}unitree_go2_real/scripts/lio_input.py) and [point_lio_go2.yaml]({url}unitree_go2_real/config/point_lio_go2.yaml): vendor deskewed clouds transformed back into base_link; padding/body removed; eight messages accumulated per estimator update; LiDAR gyro rotated into body axes; startup stationary gyro bias; accelerometer values zero and gravity disabled. The original [point_lio_unilidar package]({url}third_party/point_lio_unilidar/CMakeLists.txt) was built in a separate review workspace without source patches.",'','The optional bridge applies accepted planar LIO corrections to the high-rate vendor trajectory. Output z, roll and pitch remain the vendor values; near-zero returned height is not independent validation of LIO vertical accuracy.','','## Original-code verification','',f"Default mode: original RealTfBridge.on_odom called offline for every one of {raw['samples']:,} recorded vendor messages. Only ROS publishers/clock/logger were replaced by passive sinks. Clock offset logic and pose correction code were unchanged. With yaw_scale=1.0, the largest pose-value difference from the original input is {raw['identity_callback_matches_original_pose_max_absolute_difference']:.3g}; this verifies that the harness preserves the identity path.",'',f"Optional input: original LioInput callbacks called in full recorded receipt order. Startup gyro bias measured from this recording: `{adapter['gyro_bias_raw_frame_rad_s']}` rad/s in its original frame. First converted cloud at {adapter['first_cloud_source_s']:.3f} s, first converted IMU {adapter['first_imu_source_s']:.3f} s. Clouds rejected for no vendor pose within 20 ms: {adapter['clouds_dropped_for_missing_nearby_pose']}. Original acquisition stamps and both recording gaps were retained.",'',f"The separate replay used the repository's original Point-LIO profile and original real_tf_bridge code with pose_source=lio. Only passive audit counters were added through a subclass. Changes for isolation were limited to simulated clock/remappings; there was no filter/noise/extrinsic tuning. Replay: localhost DDS domain 210, 0.5x, no commands. End reason `{a['replay']['stop_reason']}`; source/application file hashes unchanged: {a['replay']['source_and_application_files_unchanged']}. Input observer exact stamp delivery: `{a['replay']['input_delivery_exact']}`.",'',f"The bridge's recorded source-odometry callback sequence was matched to raw output position/quaternion values, then used to recover exact source times for the re-stamped hybrid output. Verified raw sequence identity: {hy['raw_output_sequence_matches_input_exactly']}; {hy['source_odom_messages_observed_by_bridge']:,} callback outputs.",'','## Guard behavior at the recording dropout','',f"Guard limits from the original code: corrections moving the pose by more than {guard['guard_limits']['position_m']:.1f} m or {guard['guard_limits']['heading_deg']:.0f} degrees against the previous accepted correction are rejected. Total accepted {guard['accepted']}, rejected {guard['rejected']}, unmatched {guard['unmatched']}. First rejection at {guard['first_rejection_source_s']} s; last accepted at {guard['last_accepted_source_s']} s. After 44 s: `{guard['events_after_44s']}`.",'','The optional Point-LIO also diverges across the roughly four-second recording gap. The bridge rejects the large correction instead of passing it through, keeping its last accepted correction and continuing vendor odometry. The published hybrid trajectory therefore must not be presented as proof that raw Point-LIO stayed accurate. Details: [bridge_audit.json](results/bridge_audit.json).','','## Cross-check against the earlier measured-distance recordings','','The same original default yaw-correction callback was also applied to the earlier straight-distance bags; the parameter was unchanged.','','| Bag | Raw vendor 3 m / 5 m | Repo-corrected vendor 3 m / 5 m |','|---|---:|---:|']
